<title>UK: DePfa prices 1.0 bln mark five-yr Pfandbrief bond.</title>
<headline>DePfa prices 1.0 bln mark five-yr Pfandbrief bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond, announced earlier by joint lead managers Bayerische Vereinsbank, Commerzbank and Goldman Sachs, has been priced.</p>
<p> BORROWER   DEUTSCHE PFANDBRIEF- UND HYPOTHEKENBANK AG</p>
<p> AMT    1.0 BLN DEM   COUPON     4.75	MATURITY    28.JAN.02</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  100.625   PAY DATE    28.JAN.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  2.00	REOFFER    98.875    SPREAD	+42 BP</p>
<p> MOODY	AAA	 LISTING    FFT	 PAY FREQ    =</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  =	   DENOMS (K) ONE	 SALE LIMITS US/UK/DE</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ  *IPMA 2</p>
<p> GOV LAW    GERMAN    HOME CTRY  GERMANY   TAX PROVS NO GROSS UP</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.25	SELL CONC  1.75	PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p> UNDERLYING GOVT BOND AUGUST 2001 BOBL 120</p>
<p> NOTES	PFANDBRIEF SERIES 420</p>
<p>	     *WITH CONSULTATION</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
